  "answer": "Changes made (only in the two writable files):\n\n**`registry.mjs`** — rewritten `resolveFromRegistry`:\n- Validates `path` first: non-string, empty, or not starting with `/` throws `TypeError`.\n- Scans all records once, collecting the **first** static match, the **first** dynamic match, and the **first** fallback independently, then returns in precedence order: static → dynamic → fallback → `null`. This fixes the old bug where a fallback (or an earlier dynamic) short-circuited the loop.\n- Static matching is exact string equality (case sensitive, trailing slash significant); dynamic matching splits on `/`, requires equal segment counts, literal segments must match exactly, and `:name` captures the original nonempty segment value into a fresh `params` object.\n- Every returned object/`params` is newly created per call; records are never mutated. Matching helpers are local to this module (the `routes/*` helpers are not writable and the old dynamic helper was reused as-is in behavior).\n\n**`entry.mjs`** — `dispatch(path)` now delegates directly to `resolveFromRegistry(path, defaultRoutes)`, dropping the `legacyResolve` pre-check so `/old/help` is no longer special-cased in the production entry point (it now resolves via the route table, i.e. fallback `not-found`). `legacy.mjs` is untouched, so `legacyResolve('/old/help')` still returns `{ route: 'legacy-help', params: {} }`.\n\nExpected behavior with the fixture: `/users/new` → `user-new` (static beats earlier dynamic), `/users/Ada` → `user-detail` with `{ id: 'Ada' }`, `/health` → `health`, `/missing` → `not-found`, and `resolveFromRegistry('/x', [])` → `null`.\n\nNot verified by execution: no test runner or shell is available in this environment, so I only reviewed the code by reading it.",
